-- title:
--   Σ-corner at level Mr meets ker j₁∩ker jᵣ trivially
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a complete discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field, $p$ a prime with $p\neq 2$ and $p$ in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a two-dimensional residual Galois representation over the residue field (a monoid homomorphism from $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ to the endomorphisms of a rank-two space, trivial on the Galois group of some number field) which is absolutely irreducible, i.e. its base change to an algebraic closure admits no proper non-zero invariant subspace. Let $S$ be a finite set of primes containing $p$, and $M\ge 1$ with all prime divisors in $S$ and $p^2\nmid M$. A subset $\mathrm{Smin}\subseteq S$ containing $p$ is assumed to consist, away from $p$, exactly of the primes at which $\bar\rho$ is ramified; the divisibility hypotheses $q\mid M$ for $q\in \mathrm{Smin}$, $q\neq p$, and for primes $q\neq p$ outside $\mathrm{Smin}$, $q\mid M\Rightarrow q^2\mid M$ and $q^2\mid M\Rightarrow q^3\nmid M$, together with unipotence of $\bar\rho$ on inertia at each $q\in\mathrm{Smin}$, $q\neq p$ (characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$) and ordinarity at $p$ when $p\mid M$, fix the type of $M$. Let $r$ be a prime with $r\notin S$, $r\nmid M$, $p\nmid r-1$, and such that for every valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $r$ and every Frobenius element $\sigma$ there, $\operatorname{tr}\bar\rho(\sigma)^2\neq(r+1)^2$. Assume weight-two cusp forms of level $M$ have an integral structure (the forms with integral $q$-expansion coefficients span over $\mathbb{C}$), and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the weight-two level-$M$ Hecke algebra away from $S$ to the residue field with $\operatorname{charpoly}\bar\rho(\sigma)=X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$ for every prime $\ell\nmid M$, $\ell\notin S$ and Frobenius $\sigma$ at $\ell$. Put $L=Mr$. Let $\mathbb{T}$ be a commutative $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, module-finite over $\mathcal{O}$, acting $\mathcal{O}$-compatibly on $H^1(L,\top;\mathcal{O})$, the group of additive homomorphisms from $\Gamma_0(L)$ (written additively) to $\mathcal{O}$, let $\mathrm{Sp}$ be an idempotent splitting of $\mathbb{T}$ (complete orthogonal idempotents $e_j$ and maximal ideals $\mathfrak{m}_j$ exhausting the maximal ideals, with $e_j\in\mathfrak{m}_k$ iff $j\neq k$) and $i$ an index, with the corner $e_i\cdot H^1(L,\top;\mathcal{O})$ finite and free over $\mathcal{O}$. Functions $\mathrm{tfull}$ and $\mathrm{cfull}$ on the generator type (symbols $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid L$, $U_q$ for primes $q\mid L$, and diamonds $\langle d\rangle$ for $d\in(\mathbb{Z}/L)^\times$), with values in $\mathbb{T}$ and in $\mathcal{O}$, are assumed to satisfy: $\mathbb{T}$ acts on $H^1$ through the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra generated by the operators attached to the guarded generators (those whose $U_q$ components have $q\mid M$); $\mathrm{tfull}\,g$ acts as the operator attached to $g$ for guarded $g$; $\mathrm{tfull}\,g-\mathrm{cfull}\,g\in\mathfrak{m}_i$ for guarded $g$; cofullness, namely any $v$ for which all powers-to-depth conditions $(\mathrm{tfull}\,g-\mathrm{cfull}\,g)^n\cdot v\in\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}^{k}H^1$ hold, lies in the corner; $\mathrm{cfull}(T_\ell)$ reduces to $\theta(T_\ell)$; $\mathrm{cfull}(U_q)$ lies in the maximal ideal when $q\mid M$, $q\neq p$, $q^2\mid M$, while $\mathrm{cfull}(U_p)$ is a unit when $p\mid M$; and $\mathrm{cfull}(\langle d\rangle)\equiv 1$. Finally the corner is non-zero and the corresponding corner ring acts faithfully on it, and $\mathrm{LevelLE}$ data for degrees $1$ and $r$ from level $M$ to level $L$ are given. The conclusion: any $v$ in the corner with $j_1(v)=0$ and $j_r(v)=0$, where $j_d$ denotes the degeneracy map `jDegL` of degree $d$ from level $L$ to level $M$ (pull-back along the degeneracy embedding followed by corestriction), is zero.
--
--   This is the cohomological form of the absence of level raising at the auxiliary prime $r$: under Ribet's non-congruence condition $\operatorname{tr}\bar\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_r)^2\neq(r+1)^2$, the $\Sigma$-corner of $H^1(\Gamma_0(Mr),\mathcal{O})$ contains no non-zero $r$-new class. It feeds the comparison of the corner at the auxiliary level $Mr$ with the corner at level $M$ and the bound on the $\mathcal{O}$-rank of the former by twice the latter.
